WHAT "THE SOFTWARE" COVERS

The MIT grant above applies to the source of devtool.fyi: the Astro components,
layouts, pages and styles under src/, the Pages Function under functions/, the
build and snapshot scripts under scripts/, the workflows under .github/, and
the configuration around them. Take it, learn from it, build your own directory
with it.

WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER

The directory content is not licensed for reuse and is reserved:

  - the entries in src/data/tools.ts and the shelves in src/data/categories.ts,
    including every tagline, description, comparison table and editorial
    judgement in them,
  - the prose in docs/, README.md and the site's own pages,
  - the devtool.fyi name, wordmark and visual identity.

Those are © 2026 Renfred Alonge, all rights reserved. They are the part somebody
sat down and wrote, and the reason the site is worth reading; the machinery that
renders them is the part worth sharing.

A pull request adding or editing an entry is a contribution to that reserved
content, offered on the understanding that it becomes part of it. Everything
else you contribute is covered by the MIT grant above.

